.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \(dqserver.h\(dq

void init_bash_for_session(server_config_t *config);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Initializes the embedded bash interpreter for a new session.
This function is called once per session process, typically triggered by
a successful \f[CR]AUTH\f[R] command.
Subsequent calls are no\-ops (guarded by an internal static flag).
.PP
The initialization sequence is:
.IP "1." 3
Set \f[CR]shell_name\f[R] to \f[CR]\(dqbash\-server\(dq\f[R].
.IP "2." 3
Set \f[CR]interactive_shell\f[R] to \f[CR]0\f[R] (non\-interactive).
.IP "3." 3
Set \f[CR]login_shell\f[R] from \f[CR]config\->login_mode\f[R].
.IP "4." 3
Call bash initialization functions in order:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]initialize_shell_builtins()\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]initialize_traps()\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]initialize_signals(0)\f[R] (non\-privileged mode)
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]tilde_initialize()\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]initialize_shell_variables(shell_environment, 0)\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]initialize_job_control(0)\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]initialize_bash_input()\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]initialize_flags()\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]initialize_shell_options(0)\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]initialize_bashopts(0)\f[R]
.RE
.IP "5." 3
Set \f[CR]shell_initialized = 1\f[R].
.IP "6." 3
Source startup files based on configuration flags (see below).
.IP "7." 3
Source \f[CR]config\->init_file\f[R] if specified.
.SH Startup File Sourcing
The startup file behavior depends on the configuration:
.PP
\f[B]Login mode\f[R] (\f[CR]config\->login_mode\f[R] set,
\f[CR]config\->noprofile\f[R] not set): \- Sources
\f[CR]/etc/profile\f[R].
\- Then tries \f[CR]\(ti/.bash_profile\f[R]; if not found, tries
\f[CR]\(ti/.bash_login\f[R]; if not found, tries
\f[CR]\(ti/.profile\f[R].
.PP
\f[B]Default non\-login mode\f[R] (\f[CR]config\->norc\f[R] not set): \-
Sources \f[CR]/etc/bash.bashrc\f[R].
\- Sources \f[CR]\(ti/.bashrc\f[R].
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-norc\f[B] flag\f[R] (\f[CR]config\->norc\f[R] set): \-
Skips \f[CR]\(ti/.bashrc\f[R] and \f[CR]/etc/bash.bashrc\f[R].
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-noprofile\f[B] flag\f[R] (\f[CR]config\->noprofile\f[R]
set): \- Skips \f[CR]/etc/profile\f[R] and \f[CR]\(ti/.bash_profile\f[R]
(login mode only).
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-init\f[B] script\f[R] (\f[CR]config\->init_file\f[R]
set): \- Always sourced after standard startup files, regardless of
other flags.
.PP
Missing startup files are silently skipped.
