.SH NOTES
This function is idempotent \(en calling it multiple times has no effect
after the first successful initialization.
.PP
The function links against the main bash library
(\f[CR]cygbash\-5.1.dll\f[R]) to access all initialization routines.
These are the same routines used by the interactive \f[CR]bash\f[R]
shell during startup.
.PP
Startup files are sourced using bash\(cqs own \f[CR]source_file()\f[R]
function (from \f[CR]builtins/evalfile.c\f[R]), which properly sets up
\f[CR]return_catch\f[R] so that \f[CR]return\f[R] statements in sourced
scripts work correctly.
.PP
The \f[CR]$HOME\f[R] environment variable is used to locate
user\-specific startup files.
If \f[CR]$HOME\f[R] is not set, user startup files are skipped.
